# AGENTS.local.md — Local Environment (Template)

Copy this file as `AGENTS.local.md` (it is listed in `.gitignore` and **will not be committed**),
then fill in your own environment details.

```bash
cp AGENTS.local.md.example AGENTS.local.md
```

---

## 1. Hardware

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| GPU | `<Model>`, `<VRAM MiB>`, peak bandwidth `<GB/s>` |
| CPU | `<threads>` threads |
| RAM | MemTotal `<GiB>` / MemAvailable `<GiB>` |
| swap | `<Yes/No>` |
| `/dev/shm` | tmpfs `<size>` |
| Disk | `<Model>`, available `<GB>` |
| CUDA | `<Version>`, located at `<path>` |

## 2. Paths

```bash
export LLAMACPP_ROOT=<path to llama.cpp checkout>
export MODELS_DIR=<dir containing the target GGUF and the v8 head>
export SPARK_START=<path to your llama-server start script>
export PYTHON_ENV=<path to your python env>
```

| Purpose | Path |
|---|---|
| Target Weight | `${MODELS_DIR}/<target>.gguf` |
| v8 head (for inference) | `${MODELS_DIR}/spark-eagle3-v8.gguf` |
| v8 head (training starting point) | `datasets/v8/model.safetensors` + `v8/config.json` |

## 3. Test Environment

```
python <ver> / torch <ver> / CUDA <ver>
safetensors <ver> / gguf <ver> / numpy <ver>
llama.cpp <build>
```

## 4. Raw Measurement Data

Paste your own benchmark results here (`AGENTS.md` only references the conclusions; include the absolute values here).

## 5. Local Environment Considerations

- Required VRAM headroom and desktop space usage
- Process cleanup methods
- Other prerequisites specific to the local environment
